# ICCMC app · GitHub Pages deploy — ONLY the app file is tracked.
# Ignore everything, then explicitly allow just index.html (and this file).
# So no backend, worker, SQL, key or secret can EVER be committed here by accident —
# the OCR brain runs on Google Cloud Run and the data lives in Supabase, not here.
*
!index.html
# the admin OCR review page (its own self-contained build) — a 2nd app file, same rules:
# only the publishable Supabase key ships; RLS is the guard. Reached at /ocr.html.
!ocr.html
!.gitignore
# Cloudflare deploy config. Allowed deliberately: it holds no code, keys or
# connection details — only a project name, a date, and "serve this folder".
# Keep this list an allowlist; never replace it with broad patterns.
!wrangler.toml
# Tells Cloudflare which files must NOT be published. Critically it excludes
# .git — without it, Wrangler uploads the whole repo including history.
!.assetsignore
# The split front-end assets that index.html loads (CSS + vendored supabase + app logic).
# EXPLICIT entries only — never a broad assets/** — so nothing else can slip into the repo.
!assets/
!assets/app.css
!assets/vendor.js
!assets/app.js
# vendored docx-preview (Apache-2.0) — renders Word/Excel legal papers in-app for the review + print,
# so no server/LibreOffice is needed. Self-contained JS, no external calls. Explicit entry only.
!assets/docx-preview.min.js
# The ICCMC logo mark (SVG), shown in the login + the app header. Image only — no code/keys.
!assets/logo.svg
# GitHub Pages: serve every file verbatim (skip Jekyll processing).
!.nojekyll
# The repo map — explains which file is the app's source of truth (for contributors + a fresh Claude).
# Documentation only; .assetsignore keeps it out of the public Cloudflare deploy.
!README.md
# Cloudflare cache headers — keep the shell fresh, cache assets hard. Explicit allowlist entry.
!_headers
